## OCB-01 — all-time heat-shell theorem

Let the strict continuous-time Markov generator be `Q=-A`, with radial off-diagonal rates

`w1>w2>...>w6>0`.

For a row of the heat kernel write `p_r(t)` for the probability at cyclic distance `r=0,...,6` and define

`y_r=p_r-p_{r+1}`, `r=0,...,5`.

After changing coordinates from the seven radial probabilities to `(total mass,y_0,...,y_5)`, total mass decouples and

`ydot=M y`.

The exact symbolic `6x6` matrix is exported in `results/OCB-01_heat_shell_metzler.json`. Every off-diagonal entry is a positive difference `w_a-w_b` with `a<b`; the smallest strict margin is

`0.01306040604218794487...`.

Therefore `M` is irreducible Metzler. Since the localized initial condition has `y(0)=(1,0,...,0)`, strict positivity of `exp(tM)` gives

`p_0(t)>p_1(t)>...>p_6(t)`

for every finite `t>0`.

**New consequence:** in the Markov/heat realization, the complete ordinal six-shell carrier survives for all positive times. It is not merely a short-time derivative statement.

This theorem does not select heat as the physical dynamics.

## OCB-02 — conservative carrier windows for unitary and wave channels

Let `L=||A||=2.3421820411463004`.

For `U(t)=exp(-itA)`, off-diagonal amplitudes obey

`U_ij(t)=i t W_ij+r_ij`,

with

`|r_ij| <= exp(Lt)-1-Lt`.

Hence a shell gap `delta` is guaranteed to preserve amplitude/probability order whenever

`delta t > 2[exp(Lt)-1-Lt]`.

For `C(t)=cos(t sqrt(A))`,

`C_ij(t)=t^2 W_ij/2+r_ij`,

and

`|r_ij| <= cosh(t sqrt(L))-1-Lt^2/2`.

The resulting certified dimensionless windows are:

| record | nearest-shell order | all six shell order |
|---|---:|---:|
| unitary transition probability | `t < 0.0487555043` | `t < 0.00237634382` |
| wave amplitude/probability | `t < 0.544995102` | `t < 0.119451445` |

These are deliberately conservative theorem bounds, not fitted first-crossing times.

## OCB-03 — exact clock-free embedded-jump protocol

For a CTMC generator `Q=-A`, conditioned on leaving state `i`,

`P(next=j | leave i)=W_ij/s_i`.

Any global clock rescaling `Q -> cQ` cancels exactly.

For strict FIN the per-destination probabilities by shell are

`[0.2830715005, 0.1156674756, 0.0550672851, 0.0283255813, 0.0145341912, 0.0066679328]`.

The margin between a nearest-neighbor destination and the next shell is

`0.16740402485`.

Thus any `L_infinity` perturbation below `0.08370201243` preserves the top-two neighbor set.

A direct Hoeffding+union bound gives:

- 435 recorded exits to recover the top-two set for one prepared state at family error <=5%;
- 612 exits per state for simultaneous protection of all `12x11` destination frequencies at family error <=5%.

These are conservative finite-sample bounds, not optimized laboratory budgets.

The primary test is label-free: the two empirically dominant destinations from every state must form one connected 2-regular graph, hence an unlabeled `C12`.

After this graph is recovered, its graph distance defines the six shell groups and the quantitative shell profile can be tested without importing a cyclic coordinate.

